    "attribution": "Benjamin Diamond authored initial and correcting source commits. The correction credits Claude Fable 5.2 as co-author. All mathematical statements below are attributed to the maintained upstream book.",
    "theorem": {
      "source": "https://github.com/hodge-computer/sextics/blob/a87cbee85d54d3db7ac8ff54f782a16dcd2efcda/docs/03d-hodge-loci.md#3d8-split-quadric-sections-and-a-paired-exchange-fourfold-family",
      "hypotheses": "Smooth sextic in P5 invariant under global Y sign tau, all three paired signs s_i, and exchanges sigma_0:X0↔Y0 and sigma_1:X1↔Y1. This is a 40-coefficient family.",
      "statement": "The full tau-invariant rational fourth cohomology is supported on a divisor. More precisely the character chi positive on tau and s_i and negative on both exchanges has an algebraic projector representative supported on D×D for an H-stable divisor D.",
      "new_sector": "The simultaneous anti-exchange, paired-sign-invariant sector has Hodge type (33,102,33). Other sectors are supplied by prior paired-sign and reflection results.",
      "limits": "The source uses a smooth Fano reflection quotient of a second fourfold, its Hodge-conjecture consequence and a density argument. Its result supplies existence; the target explanation explicitly leaves the cycles, denominator, explicit certificate and formal target proof to be supplied."
    },
    "target": {
      "id": "quadric-contact-residual",
      "q": 1,
      "A": "X0^3*Y0^3",
      "previous_context": "The former motivation supplied no existence conclusion from its specified quotient-density constructions.",
      "current_context": "New why.md and provenance.json attribute certificate existence to the paired-exchange support theorem; the fixed equation has the required symmetries and the source states its reduction modulo five is smooth Fermat.",
      "acceptance_present": false,
      "unchanged_instance": true,
      "retained_limits": "The quotient-density parity obstruction and failure of the passive-parameter Jacobian family still concern those specified constructions."
    },
    "explicit_internal_corrections": [
      "Removed the false general claim that H^(3,1) of a threefold vanishes for dimension reasons, and the unneeded Leray computation of b2. The nodal restriction statement now uses primitive five-form residues pulling back to zero on the four-dimensional quadric bundle.",
      "Expanded the two-form formula through family residue symbols, blow-up transversality, fiber integration and relative de Rham duality.",
      "Revised the Baire argument to obtain a component containing an open subset of the Hodge locus, extend by analytic continuation, and choose the base point after shrinking. Cycles are parameterized in pairs with multiplicities.",
      "The correction supplies both bounds for saturated affine-cone dimension 54. The projective normal-form/saturated/quotient tuple is (39,53,36), already present in the first source commit. Incomparability with the quadratic-net and two-reflection families uses contraction ranks of an explicit member.",
      "Restored provenance checkCommand to the script generating checks.json, and made the nonconstructive scope explicit in why.md."
    ],
    "source_coverage": "Complete current Chapter 3D and Chapter 4, the full added section 3D.8 in saved before/after comparison patches, target-context patches and source commit messages.",
